hadiths[20]{hadithnumber,text}:
"151","‘Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman bin Abi Sa’id Khudri narrates from his father, Sayyiduna Abu Sa’id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: I went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) towards the mosque of Quba on a Monday. When we reached the locality of Banu Salim, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stood at the door of Sayyiduna ‘Itban bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) and called him. He came out dragging his lower garment. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: We have put him in a hurry. Sayyiduna ‘Itban (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Messenger of Allah! If a person hastily separates from his wife and no semen is discharged, what is the ruling (i.e., is ghusl obligatory or not)? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: The use of water is due to the emission of water (i.e., ghusl becomes obligatory only when semen is discharged)."
"152","`Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) said that` a group of the Muhajirun and Ansar differed regarding this issue (the obligation of ghusl). The Ansar said that ghusl becomes obligatory only when semen spurts out and ejaculation occurs, while the Muhajirun said that ghusl becomes obligatory when a man has intercourse with a woman. Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""I will satisfy you regarding this."" I got up and went to the house of Umm al-Mu'minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) and sought permission from her. When she granted permission, I said, ""O Umm al-Mu'minin, I want to ask you something, but I feel shy."" Umm al-Mu'minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said, ""Do not feel shy to ask about something which you could ask your real mother who gave birth to you. I am also your mother (because the wives of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, are the mothers of the believers)."" I said, ""From what does ghusl become obligatory?"" She said, ""You have asked a knowledgeable person. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'When a man sits between the four parts of a woman and the circumcised parts meet (i.e., the penis enters the vagina), then ghusl becomes obligatory.'"
"153","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from Umm Kulthum (may Allah be pleased with her), and she narrated from Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said: A man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), ""If a man has intercourse with his wife but is unable to ejaculate, is ghusl (ritual bath) obligatory on both of them?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied, ""I and she (meaning Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her) do this, and then we perform ghusl."
"154","It is narrated from Ishaq bin Abi Talha that Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Sayyidah Umm Sulaym (may Allah be pleased with her)—and she was the grandmother of the narrator of the hadith, Ishaq bin Abi Talha—came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) was also sitting there. She (Umm Sulaym) said, “O Messenger of Allah! If a woman sees in her sleep what a man sees (i.e., experiences a discharge of semen), what is the ruling?” Upon hearing this, Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said, “O Umm Sulaym! You have disgraced women (because only a very lustful woman would have a wet dream and discharge semen). May dust be upon your hands!” (And she said this as a good thing.) The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “O Aisha! May dust be upon your hands,” and he said to Umm Sulaym, “O Umm Sulaym! When a woman sees such a thing, then in that case she should perform ghusl (ritual bath).”"
"155","Umm al-Mu’minin Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her) says, ""I placed water for the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) to perform ghusl after janabah. He first washed both hands two or three times, then put his hand into the vessel and poured water over his private part and washed it with his left hand. Then he rubbed his left hand forcefully on the ground to clean it, then performed wudu as he would for prayer, then poured three handfuls of water over his head, then washed his entire body, then moved from that place and washed his feet. Then I brought a cloth (towel) for him to wipe his body, but the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) did not take it."
"156","Abu Salamah bin Abdur Rahman (the foster nephew of Sayyidah Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her) says: I and the foster brother of Ummul Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (Abdullah bin Yazid) went to her and asked about the ritual bath (ghusl) of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, after sexual impurity. She called for a vessel that could hold a sa’ (a measure) of water, and she performed ghusl behind a curtain between us and herself, and she poured water over her head three times. Abu Salamah said that the wives of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, used to cut their hair and keep it up to their ears. (The pure wives did this after the passing of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, to abandon adornment, because hair is an adornment for women.)"
"157","Narrated from Sayyida Umm Hani bint Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with her) that in the year Makkah was conquered, she came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) while he was in the higher part of Makkah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up to take a bath, so Sayyida Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her) screened him with a cloth. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) wrapped himself in his garment and then prayed eight units (rak‘ahs) of the forenoon (Duha) prayer."
"158","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) from Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The people of Bani Israel used to bathe naked and would look at each other's private parts. But Musa (peace be upon him) used to bathe alone. The people said that Musa (peace be upon him) does not bathe with us because he suffers from a hernia (i.e., swollen testicles). Once, Musa (peace be upon him) went to bathe and placed his clothes on a stone. The stone (by Allah's command) ran away with his clothes. Musa (peace be upon him) chased after it, saying, ""O stone, give me my clothes! O stone, give me my clothes!"" until the people of Bani Israel saw his private parts and said, ""By Allah! He has no disease."" At that moment, the stone stopped, and he was seen thoroughly. Then he picked up his clothes and (in anger) began to strike the stone. Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) said: By Allah! There are marks of six or seven blows of Musa (peace be upon him) on that stone."
"159","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man should not look at the 'awrah (private parts that must be covered) of another man, nor should a woman look at the 'awrah of another woman. And a man should not lie with another man under a single garment, nor should a woman lie with another woman under a single garment."
"160","Narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was carrying stones with the people for the construction of the Ka'bah, and he (peace be upon him) was wearing an izar (waist cloth). Sayyiduna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), who was his (peace be upon him) uncle, said, ""O my nephew! If you take off your izar and put it on your shoulder, it will be better."" He (peace be upon him) took off his izar and put it on his shoulder, and immediately he fainted and fell down. After that day, he (peace be upon him) was never seen naked."
"161","It is narrated from Sayyida Mu'adhah (may Allah be pleased with her) that Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and I used to perform ghusl from the same vessel, which was placed between me and him. He (peace and blessings be upon him) would take water quickly, to the extent that I would say, ""Leave some water for me."" (Sayyida Mu'adhah), the narrator of the hadith, says: And both of them would be in a state of janabah."
"162","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was in a state of major ritual impurity and wanted to eat or sleep, he would perform ablution as he did for prayer."
"163","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abi Qais that I asked Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) about the Witr of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), then she narrated the hadith (regarding Witr). I asked, ""What would the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) do in the state of janabah? Would he perform ghusl before sleeping or would he sleep before performing ghusl?"" She said that he (peace and blessings be upon him) did both; sometimes he would perform ghusl and then sleep, and sometimes he would perform wudu and then sleep. I said, ""All praise is due to Allah who has provided flexibility in this matter."
"164","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri رضي الله عنه narrates that the Messenger of Allah صلى الله عليه وسلم said: When any one of you has intercourse with his wife, then wishes to have intercourse again, he should perform ablution (and then have intercourse again)."
"165","Narrated from Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her): We set out on a journey with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When we reached al-Bayda or Dhat al-Jaysh (al-Bayda and Dhat al-Jaysh are names of places between Khaybar and Madinah), my necklace broke and fell off. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed to look for it, and the people also stayed. There was no water there, nor did the people have any water with them. The people came to Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) and said, “Do you not see what Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) has done? She has held up the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the people, where there is no water and the people have no water.” Hearing this, Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) came, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had laid his head on my thigh and was sleeping. He said, “You have held up the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the people, where there is no water and the people have no water.” He became angry and said what Allah willed, and began poking me in my side with his hand. I would have moved, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had his head on my thigh, so I did not move. Then he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slept until morning came and there was absolutely no water. Then Allah, the Exalted, revealed the verse of tayammum, so everyone performed tayammum. Usaid bin Hudair (may Allah be pleased with him), who was among the leaders, said, “O family of Abu Bakr! This is not the first blessing that has come to you (meaning, Allah has always given benefit to the Muslims because of you, and this too is a blessing received through you).” Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said: Then we made the camel on which I was riding stand up, and the necklace was found underneath it."
"166","Shaqiq says: I was sitting with Sayyiduna Abdullah (bin Mas'ud) and Sayyiduna Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with them both. Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""O Abu Abdur Rahman"" (this is the kunyah of Ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with them both), ""if a person is in a state of janabah and does not find water for a month, what should he do about prayer?"" Sayyiduna Abdullah said, ""Even if he does not find water for a month, he should not perform tayammum."" Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""Then what is the ruling about the verse in Surah Al-Ma'idah: 'If you do not find water, then perform tayammum with clean earth'?"" Sayyiduna Abdullah said, ""If by this verse they are allowed to perform tayammum in the state of janabah, then gradually, they will start performing tayammum even when water is cold."" Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""Have you not heard the hadith of Sayyiduna Ammar (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sent me on an errand, and there I became junub and did not find water, so I lay down in the dust as an animal does. After that, I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and informed him, so he (peace and blessings be upon him) said, 'It would have been sufficient for you to do like this with both your hands.' Then he struck the earth once with both hands and struck the left hand on the right hand, then wiped the back of the hands and the face."" Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""You know that Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was not satisfied with the hadith of Sayyiduna Ammar (may Allah be pleased with him)."" (Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, were of the opinion that tayammum is not sufficient for janabah. But it is proven from ahadith that they later retracted this view.)"
"167","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Umair, the freed slave of Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that: I and Abdur Rahman bin Yasar, who was the freed slave of Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her), the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), went to Abu Juham bin Harith. Abu Juham said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came from the direction of Bi’r Jamal (a place near Madinah). On the way, a man met him and greeted him with Salam. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not reply to him until he came to a wall, wiped his face and both hands, and then replied to the Salam."
"168","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that he met the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, on one of the roads of Madinah while he was in a state of major ritual impurity (junub), so he slipped away and went to perform ghusl (ritual bath). The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, noticed his absence, and when he returned, he asked, ""Where were you?"" He replied, ""O Messenger of Allah! When you met me, I was in a state of major impurity, and I disliked sitting with you without having performed ghusl."" The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said, ""Subhan Allah! Does a believer ever become impure?"
"169","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to remain engaged in the remembrance of Allah at all times and in every condition."
"170","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came out of the toilet and food was brought. People reminded him about ablution, so he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Am I about to pray that I should perform ablution?"
